# Local configuration — copy to ".env" and adjust.
# .env is listed in .gitignore and is NEVER committed.
#
# BOTH values are OPTIONAL: PoE-VIEW2 has working defaults and runs
# without any .env file. You only need this file if you want to
# override one of the values on purpose (e.g. for your own fork).

# OAuth client ID of the app registered with GGG (public client, PKCE).
# Default: "poeview" — already registered, works out of the box.
#POE_CLIENT_ID=poeview

# Contact address for the User-Agent header (required by GGG). Per the
# GGG docs, it identifies the APPLICATION, not the individual user —
# as a regular user you don't need to set this.
# Default: the project address from poe_view/config.py.
# Set your own address here if you fork PoE-VIEW2 and distribute it
# yourself, so GGG inquiries reach the right person.
#POE_CONTACT_EMAIL=your@email.example
